# Check out LF on every platform. Without this, Windows rewrites files to CRLF
# on checkout, which changes their bytes - and the ?v= stamps in the HTML are
# sha1 hashes of those bytes. A checkout on a different machine would then
# recompute every hash, restamp every page, and force all visitors to
# re-download files that never actually changed.
#
# This is not theoretical here. public/css/style.min.css contains a newline, so
# it really would convert:
#
#   as LF    12405 bytes  sha1 2f829250
#   as CRLF  12406 bytes  sha1 296de5ab
#
# Every site copied from this kit inherits the same ?v= scheme, so it inherits
# the same exposure. Keep this file in the copy.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch binaries
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
